[12:06:58] I've redrawn the doctor with stethoscope as a Solo48 model, and it validates as `valid` with no warnings. To make it fit, the stethoscope now hangs around the neck instead of floating inside the chest as the trace had it.

**What it is:** a front-facing bust (a round head above a rounded shoulder shape) with a stethoscope around the neck. The tubes come down from the shoulders into a U, and the round chestpiece hangs from the bottom of the U. Everything is mirrored on x=24.

**Shape: tall rectangle (VRECT_L) instead of the suggested square.** The square is 36 units tall. That's not enough to stack the head, the 8-unit gap under it, the U and a chestpiece ring while keeping every gap at 8 and every hole at least 6. VRECT_L gives 40 units, and the trace was taller than wide (0.87) anyway. Every edge of the drawing sits exactly on the shape's box.

**Metric issues:**

| Issue | Result |
|---|---|
| e0/e1 head too close to shoulders (2.77) | Fixed: head bottom y=16, neckline y=24, exactly 8 on centerlines (4 units of visible gap) |
| head-gap e2/e4 | Not a real issue: the metrics read the chestpiece ring as a head. The actual head now has the exact 8-unit gap, and the figure is marked as a person in the model. |
| e1/e2, e1/e3, e1/e4, e2/e3 stethoscope crowding the shoulders and itself | Fixed by redesign (below) |
| keyshape-short-axis | Fixed: all four edges touch the VRECT_L box |
| stroke-width (info) | Drawn at stroke 4 from the start |

**What I dropped and why:** the trace's stethoscope had earpiece hooks, a U, a lower loop and a ring off to the right. At 8-unit spacing that needs about 44 units of width, and the chest is only 32–36 wide. So the tubes now hang from the shoulder joints at (18,24) and (30,24), and the ring (radius 5) hangs centred at the bottom. The earpiece hooks and side loop are gone. This is the one part I couldn't keep from the reference.

**Checks:** I looked at it at 48 px in light and dark themes after comparing three candidates, and kept the one with the radius-6 head, since the other two read like a tie or figure-8. The head and shoulders follow the project's bust reference (`user.svg`). I didn't use a Lucide icon as a model.

As asked, nothing was registered under `icon_set/model/icons`, `published/` wasn't touched, and the build and gallery weren't run.

Files are in `new-pipeline-test/output_png/20260930-1155-doctor-with-stethoscope/`:
- doctor_with_stethoscope_redraw.py
- doctor-with-stethoscope_redraw.svg
- doctor-with-stethoscope_redraw.png
- doctor-with-stethoscope_redraw-48.png

